.TH VAPORWAVE-WSL2 1 "2026-09-02" "realisateur" "standup runbook"
.SH NAME
vaporwave\-wsl2 \- stand a SECOND self\-dev host up as a WSL2 distro on dexter
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
./constate.sh                              is it a self\-dev host yet?
./constate.sh \-\-target wsl:vaporwave       the rescue route, before sshd answers
dresse \-\-host \-\-on vaporwave \-\-check       what the machine still needs
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
`svc\-vaporwave' has run `aedile' and `vkv\-inventory' out of a uid\-1001 service
account on mandark, outside every sensor this estate has: the status page cannot
see it (bin/monkey\-status\-collect.py reads uid 3000\-3099), it has no ROSTER row,
no tempo, no usage gate and no App attribution. Its last reports are 2026\-08\-01
and 2026\-07\-18. This stands it up the way monkey is stood up, so it is watched
by the same things.
.PP
.B THIS IS NOT MONKEY'S MIGRATION.
That runbook moved a live 27G machine and its whole risk was preserving identity;
this imports a stock rootfs and creates nothing that has to survive. So it is
short, and what it inherits is the HAZARD LIST, which was paid for once already
and does not need paying again.
.SH WHAT IT COSTS TO GET WRONG, MEASURED ON dexter 2026\-09\-02
.nf
ONE NETWORK NAMESPACE for every distro. A distro's ports are the estate's.
  in use: 53 2223 2224 8000 8080 8090 8643. 2225 is FREE and is ours.
  22 is NOT free \- Windows sshd holds it, which is why monkey took 2224.
TWO DISTROS EXIST: Ubuntu (DEFAULT) and monkey. A bare `wsl \-d' with no name
  hits Ubuntu, WHICH CARRIES ZACH'S CHANNEL. Name the distro in every command.
C: 81.5G free, D: 2621G (measured 2026\-09\-03T05:08Z). The guest disk goes on
  C: (realisateur#274/#275: D: is the WD Elements USB that logged 1580
  controller errors in a week and took all 14 accounts down). Tarballs are
  bulk scratch and belong on D:. A stock rootfs needs ~2\-3G, so space is not
  a constraint on this standup. It was one for a day: C: was 28G free and 95%
  full until realisateur#941 accepted the cutover and reclaimed 54G by
  deleting the monkey/crt\-vm/nomac VMs and uninstalling VirtualBox.
  VIRTUALBOX IS GONE FROM dexter, and so is `nomac' \- so the 2026\-08\-04
  brief's plan to put these projects on that VM has no host left to name.
.fi
.PP
.B \-\-shutdown IS NOT AVAILABLE.
It stops EVERY distro including Ubuntu, which carries the container stack that
IS the channel to Zach, and dexter's sshd on 2223.
.B wsl \-\-terminate vaporwave
is safe and is the only stop this runbook uses. Anything that must restart WSL
is driven from PORT 22, the Windows route, which is the only one that survives.
.PP
.B NO TAILSCALE IN THE DISTRO.
A kernel\-TUN tailscaled lands a `ts\-input' chain in the SHARED namespace
carrying `\-s 100.64.0.0/10 ! \-i tailscale0 \-j DROP', which drops tailnet
traffic arriving on dexter's own mirrored eth0. 2223 went dead the moment
monkey booted with it. `\-\-netfilter\-mode=off' is NOT enough; the interface is
the conflict. vaporwave is reached by PORT, like monkey, and joins no tailnet.
.SH 1. THE DISTRO
ON dexter, Windows route. Import a stock rootfs; there is nothing to copy.
.nf

  ssh \-p 22 \-i ~/.ssh/id_dexter_win zach@dexter.tail893f2c.ts.net
  wsl.exe \-\-install \-\-no\-launch \-d Ubuntu\-24.04   # or an exported rootfs tar
  wsl.exe \-\-import vaporwave C:\evaporwave C:\evaporwave\-rootfs.tar
  wsl.exe \-d vaporwave \-u root \-\- /bin/true
.fi
.PP
.B The first boot is the window with no systemd,
because a distro with no /etc/wsl.conf does not start it. Write the file, then
restart the distro by name:
.nf

  [boot]
  systemd=true
  [user]
  default=zach
  [network]
  hostname=vaporwave
.fi
.SH 2. THE PORT, AND WHY IT IS THE IDENTITY
The namespace is shared, so the PORT selects the host, not the name. Bind 2225
and list BOTH address families \- a bare `ListenStream=2225' binds [::] only and
the route is refused. In /etc/systemd/system/ssh.socket.d/override.conf:
.nf

  [Socket]
  ListenStream=
  ListenStream=0.0.0.0:2225
  ListenStream=[::]:2225
.fi
.PP
Then, from mandark, prove the port selects the host rather than assuming it:
.nf

  ssh\-keyscan \-p 2225 dexter.tail893f2c.ts.net   # ours
  ssh\-keyscan \-p 2224 dexter.tail893f2c.ts.net   # monkey's
.fi
.PP
.B Two identical keys means NOTHING is listening on 2225
and the address fell through to something else in the namespace. That is the
hazard that cost monkey a week, and `./constate.sh' grades exactly this row.
.SH 3. THE HOST, DRIVEN FROM mandark
.nf

  dresse \-\-host \-\-on vaporwave \-\-check     # writes nothing
  dresse \-\-host \-\-on vaporwave \-\-apply     # remote sudo \-n, not local root
.fi
.PP
Nothing of ours is installed to run this. `dresse' ships each step and the
`lib/' it sources to a mktemp \-d and removes it, so the host ends up holding
the pinned verb build and nothing else \- realisateur#886's invariant, not a
second /root/realisateur\-refresh.
.B The verb build is NOT a prerequisite:
a greenfield host has none, which is why the tool that stands it up cannot be
delivered by the channel that standing it up installs (realisateur#545).
.SH 4. THE ACCOUNTS
One unix user per project in uid 3000\-3099, the band realisateur#102 reserves.
.B svc\-vaporwave's uid 1001 is NOT reused
\- it is outside the band every sensor reads, which is the whole reason its work
has been invisible.
.PP
Tier 1, `hf7y'\-owned and unblocked: `dog', `vibe\-kiosk', `inv\-redirects',
`vkv23'. Run `setup\-selfdev\-project.sh' per account ON the host until
realisateur#895's second half lands.
.PP
.B Tier 2 is gated, and NOT on the thing the 2026\-08\-04 brief said.
`wavebucks' (which is where `aedile' actually lives), `inventory\-app',
`nomac.org' and `CodeDumpster' belong to `media\-arts\-collective'.
.PP
That brief required TYLER'S BUY\-IN, and it was right to: it proposed adding a
project user to `nomac', HIS OFFICE HOST, sharing its 4G/2vCPU and 103G disk
beside `romulus'. That host does not exist \- realisateur#941 deleted it. What
is left is a GitHub ORG, and Zach is an `admin' of it (measured 2026\-09\-03;
admins are adamdavies1915, bobtheavenger42, hf7y).
.B So Tyler is not a gate on this, and carrying that requirement forward was
.B an error: the question moved hosts and narrowed, and the old answer was
.B repeated instead of re\-derived.
.PP
What IS still owed, measured rather than asserted:
.nf
1  a second App installation, on media\-arts\-collective. Zach can do it \-
   he is an org admin. Not a code change.
2  cred_own_repo() in bin/lib/selfdev\-credentials\-set.sh is `printf %s "$1"' \-
   identity, with no owner in it at all. That is ALREADY realisateur#916,
   filed because `apms' is not `apms\-2173'. A repo in a second org is the
   same defect one step further on, not a new one.
.fi
.PP
.B It is NOT "make the estate multi\-owner".
GH_ESTATE_OWNER is one overridable variable (bin/lib/estate\-set.sh), and the
only `hf7y' strings left outside it are prose \- a usage line, an exit\-ladder
citation, and an etalon workflow ref. bin/lib/registry\-set.sh records that the
roster half already resolves a project through its conf REPO_URL, which is the
seam to use.
.SH 5. THE CREDENTIAL, LAST AND BY HAND
The second identity ALREADY EXISTS and does not need buying: it is the
.B nomac OAuth,
held by `svc\-vaporwave' on mandark (Zach, 2026\-09\-03). It is independent of
the `nomac' VM, which no longer exists \- realisateur#941 deleted it with the
rest of VirtualBox. Nothing about that deletion touches the Anthropic account.
.PP
.B WHICH COPY IS THE RIGHT COPY, because the rule cuts both ways.
Bringing svc\-vaporwave's OWN credential across is the whole point: that IS the
second quota. Bringing monkey's or zach's across silently merges the second
quota back into the first, which is the one thing this is being bought to
avoid. So:
.nf

  from svc\-vaporwave, or a fresh login AS the account   CORRECT
  from /etc/selfdev/claude\-token on monkey              WRONG, merges the quotas
  from zach, or into any group\-readable path            WRONG
.fi
.PP
.B AN AGENT DOES NOT FETCH IT.
`/home/svc\-vaporwave' is 0700 and its contents are unreadable to anyone but
root and that account, which is correct and is not an obstacle to work around.
CLAUDE.md: an agent that needs a credential stops and asks, and never goes
looking. Zach either moves the file or logs in again as the account on
vaporwave; `dresse' only ever \-\-checks it, and
.B selfdev\-claude\-token.sh \-\-install
takes a file a human supplies.
.PP
.B AND REVOKE THE PAT THAT COMES WITH THE NAME.
senechal#279 recorded that svc\-vaporwave's GitHub PAT is over\-scoped
(`admin:org'), expires 2027\-07\-20, and is registered nowhere. It is a GitHub
credential, not this one, and it must not be inherited by the accounts standing
up here \- they push as the App. `selfdev\-credentials.sh \-\-audit' walks the
self\-dev band only, so nothing has been watching it.
.SH 6. ARMING, WHICH IS A SEPARATE ACT
`schedule/ROSTER' in hf7y/scheduler gains `<project> | <account>@vaporwave' rows.
Only a human edits the `state' column; that edit IS the arming. Leave them
`parked' until the account has run clean once.
.PP
The watcher is already generic: bin/monkey\-watch.sh parameterises VM,
MONKEY_HOST, MONKEY_PORT, SSH_KEY, STATE_FILE and PUBLISH_DIR (default
`monkey'), so a second instance publishes hf7y.com/vaporwave/status.json on env
alone. `ausculte' is NOT generic \- its hosts, arming, hygiene and fleet probes
read monkey's status URL or ssh ${AUSCULTE_FLEET_HOST:\-monkey} \- so a second
host is invisible to the witness until that becomes a set. That is the real
cost of symmetry and it belongs here, not in a later pass.
.SH ROLLBACK
`wsl.exe \-\-terminate vaporwave' then `wsl.exe \-\-unregister vaporwave'. Nothing
else on dexter is touched by any step above, and no account on monkey is
modified, so there is nothing else to undo.
